    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## SlopeCycle Interview Analyst\nEvery 5 minutes (or when someone presses **Run now**) this looks in the Google Drive **Inbox** folder, asks our local processor what is new, hands each new file to the processor, and writes the answers into the Google Sheet.\n\n**n8n only moves things around. The processor decides everything** (duplicates, checks, retries).\n\nBefore first use: open **Settings** and paste in your Inbox folder id and Sheet id.",
        "height": 260,
        "width": 560,
        "color": 4
      },
      "id": "31711d86-9e99-5da8-9249-ff3137f4afb5",
      "name": "Note: Start here",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -20,
        -330
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "### 1. Two ways to start\nThe timer fires every 5 minutes. The **Run now button** is a web address (POST /webhook/slopecycle-run-now) that answers right away and starts the same path.",
        "height": 560,
        "width": 280,
        "color": 7
      },
      "id": "50dfbd48-8ca7-5f0d-a87d-3d0c41f842b2",
      "name": "Note: 1 Triggers",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -20,
        -40
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "### 2. Settings (one place)\nInbox folder id, Sheet id and the processor address live ONLY here. Change them here and nowhere else.",
        "height": 330,
        "width": 280,
        "color": 7
      },
      "id": "62ca8598-2fc7-578e-b116-f6f521b2b3b2",
      "name": "Note: 2 Settings",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        280,
        -40
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "### 3. Look in the Inbox\nLists only the files directly inside the Inbox folder (not sub-folders), skipping trashed files, then puts them in one list.",
        "height": 330,
        "width": 520,
        "color": 7
      },
      "id": "63709f96-4bf1-5a53-b113-5d35898f65db",
      "name": "Note: 3 Inbox",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        580,
        -40
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "### 4. Ask the processor what to do\nSends the whole file list to the processor. It answers with only the files that are new or changed, and for each one says what to do (**process**, **reject** or **rewrite**).",
        "height": 330,
        "width": 800,
        "color": 7
      },
      "id": "32b06318-443e-5a96-9032-6dc617bbf245",
      "name": "Note: 4 Plan",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        1100,
        -40
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "### 5. One file at a time, then hand to the processor\nThe processor runs one local AI model, so files go one by one.\n- **process**: download the file (Google Docs become plain text) and send it.\n- **reject / rewrite**: no file needed, just send the decision.\nThis step can take up to an hour for audio.",
        "height": 520,
        "width": 1100,
        "color": 7
      },
      "id": "8f54a22a-0a3a-5583-bdb0-6732b3092013",
      "name": "Note: 5 One at a time",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        1900,
        -120
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "### 6. Save to the Google Sheet (in this order)\nTranscripts, then Evidence, then Interviews, then Run Log. A step with nothing to save is skipped. Each row is added, or updated if its id is already there, so a retry never makes a duplicate. Only the columns the processor sends are written; any extra columns your team adds to a tab are left alone.",
        "height": 220,
        "width": 3000,
        "color": 7
      },
      "id": "da486af0-845b-597d-a4b6-c0ac3e4d223f",
      "name": "Note: 6 Sheet",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        3180,
        -120
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "### 7. Tell the processor how it went\nAll saves worked: **save finished** (the processor then marks the file done).\nA save failed: **save failed** with the error message (the processor will retry later). Either way we carry on with the next file.",
        "height": 360,
        "width": 560,
        "color": 7
      },
      "id": "4d5871c8-c6e6-5dba-b0ce-0a73aa4f6270",
      "name": "Note: 7 Report",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        6800,
        -120
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "If the download or the processor call fails, we skip to the next file. The processor notices the file was never finished and offers it again later.",
        "height": 130,
        "width": 560,
        "color": 3
      },
      "id": "04a47dbe-d39c-53c0-b0a6-f31615b3d120",
      "name": "Note: Failures",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        2400,
        420
      ]
    }
  ],
